{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The deviation is established on the platform's own recorded distances: the trip record gives an actual distance of 9.9 km against a recommended route of 8.3 km, a deviation of 1.60 km, which is over POL-RD-22's 1.0 km tolerance and is recorded as not within tolerance. This is not a within-tolerance case, so the driver cannot rely on POL-RD-24 rows (c) or (e) to keep the whole fare.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05016", "EV-GPS-05016"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-22"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.derived.v7.deviation.deviation_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-RD-21 required the driver to inform the rider of the deviation by in-app chat before or at the point of deviation. The complete chat log holds exactly two messages, at 18:21:17 and 18:21:57, both about the pickup ('waiting at the library drop-off', 'thanks coming'), and the deviation was detected later at 18:27:35. The driver had a working, read-and-answered in-app channel minutes earlier and said nothing about the reroute on it.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-05016", "EV-TRIP-05016"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-21"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.derived.v7.messages_during_trip.messages",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The trip record carries an empty in_app_calls list, so the driver's account of a verbal notice has no call recording behind it. Under POL-RD-21 a verbal notice with no recording cannot be established, and under POL-GEN-26 no inference may be drawn from that absence. The notification obligation therefore fails on this record.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05016", "EV-CHAT-05016"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-21", "POL-GEN-26"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.in_app_calls",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The traffic justification is not made out on POL-RD-23's terms. POL-RD-23 justifies a reroute only where a TRAFFIC_ADVISORY intersects the recommended route and overlaps the trip window; the advisory's own derived facts leave the route intersection undetermined (intersects_route: null, with the express reason that 'the record does not say whether this advisory lies on the recommended route'), so the intersection element is not established and the reroute is not traffic-justified.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-05016-01", "EV-TRIP-05016"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-23"],
      "relies_on": "traffic_advisory.derived.v7.intersects_route",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "In the alternative, even taking the driver's traffic case at its highest, POL-RD-24 row (b) governs: traffic-justified, rider not informed, deviation over 1 km, which prescribes a refund of the excess distance fare rather than retention. Row (a) — the only row that withholds money — requires that the rider was informed and agreed, and the chat log shows no notification and no agreement, so row (a) is unavailable to the driver.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-05016", "EV-TRIP-05016"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-24"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.derived.v7.deviation.within_tolerance",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The prescribed remedy is arithmetically the present state. The excess distance fare is the deviation of 1.60 km times the per-km rate of 1.05 SGD, without surge, rounded to the cent: 1.68 SGD (POL-RD-24). The fare breakdown records refund_issued_sgd of 1.68 SGD against a PARTIALLY_REFUNDED fare, so both row (b) and row (d) are already satisfied. The driver's claim for that 1.68 SGD fails and the present state stands — the rider keeps the refund (NO_ACTION under POL-GEN-03).",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-05016", "EV-TRIP-05016"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-24", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "fare_breakdown.derived.money.excess_distance_fare_sgd",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's stated reason — that the detour was 'faster for him' — is contradicted by the trip record itself: the actual duration was 21.0 minutes against a recommended-route duration of 17.6 minutes. The deviation cost the rider time as well as distance, so it cannot be excused as a service to the rider, and the driver's own account of a beneficial reroute is unsupported by the platform's timings.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05016"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-21"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.actual_duration_min",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "This case is within the AI's remit and should be decided now rather than held: the deviation of 1.60 km is within POL-RD-25's 2 km limit for an AI ruling, and the contested value of 1.68 SGD sits below POL-GEN-22's 10.00 SGD band so the ruling is final at any confidence, with no fraud flag on either profile to raise the bar. The refund should therefore be confirmed rather than left in suspense.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05016", "EV-FARE-05016"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-25", "POL-GEN-22"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.derived.v7.deviation.over_ai_limit",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "NO_ACTION",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.85,
    "explanation": "This case was filed by the driver to get back the 1.68 SGD the platform already refunded to the rider and recovered from him. On the platform's own records that claim does not succeed, and the present state stands.\n\nWhat the records show. The trip's recorded distance was 9.9 km against a recommended route of 8.3 km (EV-TRIP-05016) — a deviation of 1.60 km. That is above POL-RD-22's 1.0 km tolerance, so the 'within tolerance' rows of the refund matrix do not apply.\n\nNotification. POL-RD-21 required the driver to tell the rider about the route change by in-app chat, or by a recorded call, before or at the point of deviation. The complete chat log (EV-CHAT-05016, weight 1.0) holds only the two pickup messages, and the trip record shows the in-app call list empty. Under POL-RD-21 a verbal notice with no recording in the record cannot be established, and the rider's account — that nothing was said about changing route — is consistent with that. The rider was therefore not informed.\n\nTraffic justification. The driver argues the heavy-traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-05016-01) sat on the recommended route and so justified the reroute; the rider argues the intersection is unproved because the artifact's intersects_route field is null and POL-RD-23 leaves that to me. I do not need to resolve it, because it does not change the outcome. If the reroute was traffic-justified, POL-RD-24 row (b) applies (justified, rider not informed, over 1 km): refund of the excess distance fare. If it was not justified, row (d) applies (not justified, over 1 km): refund of the excess distance fare in full. Both prescribe the same money, so the driver's disagreement and the rider's disagreement on this point are both moot, and no fact needed to decide the case is left unestablished (POL-GEN-26 does not bite).\n\nThe amount. POL-RD-24 fixes the excess distance fare at the deviation times the base per-km rate, without surge: 1.60 km x 1.05 SGD = 1.68 SGD. The fare breakdown (EV-FARE-05016) records exactly 1.68 SGD already refunded to the rider and recovered from the driver, with the fare marked PARTIALLY_REFUNDED. The driver is right that no more than this sum can be recovered and that it has already been taken — that is precisely why his claim to have it returned fails. The 26.34 SGD metered fare is not in issue.\n\nOutcome. Because the rider is owed the 1.68 SGD that has already been refunded, the driver's claim fails and the present state stands: NO_ACTION, with no further amounts to either side. The contested value of 1.68 SGD is below POL-GEN-22's 10.00 SGD finality band (AI final at any confidence), the deviation of 1.60 km is inside POL-RD-25's 2 km AI limit, neither profile carries a fraud flag, and the ruling meets the 0.80 confidence POL-RD-25 requires for a route deviation. No clause of this version produces a referral on a route deviation, so none is made.",
    "referrals": []
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
